  "ai_overview": {
    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Ensure personal safety first, then document the damage and prevent further water intrusion before contacting your insurance company.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "document the damage and prevent further water intrusion before contacting your insurance company"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "1. Check for Safety"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Stay off the roof: Never climb onto a damaged or wet roof, as hidden structural weakness makes it dangerous."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Watch for hazards : Check for downed power lines, broken tree limbs, or gas leaks around the property."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Keep clear: Keep children and pets away from damaged areas."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "2. Document the Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Take photos and videos: Capture wide shots of the property and close-ups of missing shingles, dents, or broken tiles."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Inspect the interior : Check ceilings, walls, and the attic for water stains, leaks, or pooling water."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Save evidence: Keep samples of fallen debris like large hail stones or broken shingle pieces if safe to collect."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "3. Prevent Further Damage (Mitigation)"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Cover leaks: Place buckets under active indoor drips and use plastic sheeting or a tarp to cover exposed roof decking from the outside if you can do so safely."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Save receipts: Keep all receipts for emergency supplies, temporary repairs, or temporary lodging, as insurance may reimburse these costs."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Act quickly: Delaying temporary fixes can lead to mold or rot, which insurance companies may refuse to cover."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "4. Contact Your Insurance Company"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "File promptly: Report the damage to your insurer within the window specified in your policy (often 60 to 90 days, though sooner is better)."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get a claim number : Write down your claim number and the name of the assigned adjuster."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Keep records: Log every conversation and keep copies of all paperwork sent and received."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "5. Hire a Reputable Contractor"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Avoid storm chasers: Beware of door-to-door contractors who appear immediately after a major storm; look for established local roofers."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Get an inspection : Ask the contractor for a detailed damage report with photos and measurements."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Meet the adjuster: Request that your contractor be present during the insurance adjuster's visit to point out all identified damage."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What type of storm hit (hail, heavy wind, fallen tree)"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Whether you see active leaks inside your home"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you prepare specific notes for your insurance call."
      }
    ],
